#. type: Title #
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remote access (Cloudflare Tunnel + Access)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:10
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> Expose Chamber WebUI to the public internet safely for **single-user** personal use.\n"
"> Prerequisites: domain on Cloudflare, Zero Trust team, Google (or other IdP) for Access login.\n"
"> Security context: [`security.md`](security.md) · install: [`install.md`](install.md)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:14
msgid ""
"FreeAnima can publish `127.0.0.1:2658` via **Cloudflare Tunnel** "
"(`cloudflared`) with **Cloudflare Access** authentication at the edge. Login "
"happens on Cloudflare (e.g. Google), not in FreeAnima."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Layer                    | Role                                                                    |\n"
"| ------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Cloudflare Access        | User login, Allow policy (your email)                                   |\n"
"| cloudflared              | Outbound tunnel to local Hub                                            |\n"
"| FreeAnima JWT middleware | Validates `Cf-Access-Jwt-Assertion`; loopback direct access still works |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quick start"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:24
msgid "One command (interactive wizard includes cloudflared install):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:25
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"anima tunnel setup\n"
"anima service start\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "Open `https://<your-hostname>/chamber/dashboard` from PC or mobile browser → sign in with Google (or configured IdP).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup wizard"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:35
msgid ""
"`anima tunnel setup` saves each answer to `~/.anima/config.yaml` as you go "
"(`tunnel.enabled` stays `false` until success). Re-run the wizard to resume "
"with saved values."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:41
msgid "Public hostname (e.g. `anima.example.com`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:41
msgid "Zero Trust team name (e.g. `myteam` → `myteam.cloudflareaccess.com`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:41
msgid "Allowed email (single-user Allow policy)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:41
msgid ""
"Optional Cloudflare API Token — auto-creates Tunnel, DNS, and Access App"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:41
msgid "Session duration (default 7 days)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:43
msgid "Secrets are stored in **pass**:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:48
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| pass 路径                                | 是什么                                                                | 谁提供                                             |\n"
"| ---------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `services/cloudflare/api-token`          | **Cloudflare API Token** — 调用 Cloudflare API 创建 Tunnel/DNS/Access | 你在 Dashboard → 我的个人资料 → API 令牌 创建      |\n"
"| `services/cloudflare/tunnel-credentials` | **隧道连接器凭证** — `cloudflared` 连接 Cloudflare 用                 | setup 通过 API 自动生成，**不要**与 API Token 混淆 |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "**不是** Zero Trust 控制台里「隧道 → 安装连接器」复制的那段令牌（那是旧版手动安装方式；本向导用 API Token 自动换取隧道凭证）。\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:52
msgid "Config is written to `~/.anima/config.yaml` under `tunnel:`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tunnel ingress targets the Hub at `127.0.0.1:<port>` where `<port>` comes from the running service (`server.status.json`) or defaults to `2658` — it is **not** a `tunnel:` config field. Use `anima service --port` for the Hub; `anima tunnel setup --port` only overrides during setup.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:55
#, no-wrap
msgid "Non-interactive"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:57
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"anima tunnel setup --non-interactive \\\n"
"  --hostname anima.example.com \\\n"
"  --team myteam \\\n"
"  --email you@gmail.com \\\n"
"  --access-api \\\n"
"  --yes\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:67
msgid ""
"Provide API Token via pass before running, or paste during interactive setup."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "Manual Access (no API Token)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:71
msgid ""
"If you skip the API Token, the wizard prints numbered Dashboard steps: "
"create self-hosted Access App, Allow-by-email policy, copy **AUD** tag into "
"`tunnel.access.audience`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:72
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:80
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Command                | Description                                               |\n"
"| ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `anima tunnel status`  | Tunnel / Access / cloudflared state                       |\n"
"| `anima tunnel start`   | Start cloudflared sidecar                                 |\n"
"| `anima tunnel stop`    | Stop sidecar                                              |\n"
"| `anima tunnel install` | Download cloudflared only (optional; setup includes this) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:82
msgid ""
"When `tunnel.enabled: true`, `anima service start` also starts the tunnel "
"sidecar (systemd user unit or foreground with `--foreground`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:83
#, no-wrap
msgid "API Token permissions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:86
msgid "创建 **API Token**（非隧道连接器令牌）时建议权限："
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:90
msgid "Account — Cloudflare Tunnel: Edit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:90
msgid "Zone — DNS: Edit (auto CNAME)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:90
msgid "Account — Access: Apps and Policies: Edit (optional `--access-api`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:99
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Symptom              | Check                                                            |\n"
"| -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Public URL 502       | Hub running? `anima service status`                              |\n"
"| Access login loop    | IdP enabled in Access App; email in Allow policy                 |\n"
"| 401 from Hub         | `tunnel.access.audience` matches Access App AUD                  |\n"
"| Local Chamber broken | Loopback bypass — use `http://127.0.0.1:2658` without CF headers |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:100
#, no-wrap
msgid "PC vs mobile"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:102
msgid ""
"Each browser keeps its own Access session cookie. First visit on PC and "
"phone each require one Google login; sessions renew per configured duration."
msgstr ""
